2,The Guiro - Everything You Need To Know | Electronic Drum Advisor,https://www.electronicdrumadvisor.com/guiro/,"The name, derivated from the ancient Maipurean language, indicates the fruit of the guira (the Calabash tree), the main material Tainos used to build the instrument.",Taíno,Maipurean
3,Taino - New World Encyclopedia,https://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Taino,"Some Taíno practiced polygamy. Men, and sometimes women, might have two or three spouses, and the caciques would marry as many as 30. Taínos spoke a Maipurean language.",Taíno,Maipurean
